/// \class SupplyCenterCreate
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Create module registered as "SupplyCenterCreate": when its
///        object's construction completes, registers the object as a supply
///        center with every player.
///
/// SupplyCenterCreate::onBuildComplete runs once (it checks and clears the
/// module's build-complete flag) and then, for every player in the player
/// list that has a resource gathering manager, hands the object to that
/// manager. This is the same loop as Zero Hour's, where the call is
/// ResourceGatheringManager::addSupplyCenter.
///
/// \par Modding
/// The module has no fields: its registration uses the generic data factory
/// described on the group page.
///
/// \see SupplyCenterCreate::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn Module *SupplyCenterCreate::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "SupplyCenterCreate": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The bare module data built by the generic data
///                    factory.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see SupplyCenterCreate


