/// \class ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Client behavior module registered as
///        "ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehavior": keeps a looping sound
///        going that is chosen by its drawable's model condition flags.
///
/// Read from the retail body as the reconstruction interprets it: when the
/// module is handed a set of model condition flags (two of its interface
/// functions do this, and the reconstruction reads them as condition-change
/// notifications), it asks its module data for the matching entry. When
/// that differs from the current one, it clears the current sound, and if
/// the new entry has a sound it starts it through TheAudio, tied to the
/// drawable, and keeps the handle. Each entry carries two sets of condition
/// flags, which the reconstruction reads as required and excluded
/// conditions. The entry and field names inside an entry are not
/// established, and no Zero Hour or BFME 1 source for the class is known.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Field (ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehaviorModuleData, from the retail
/// table): \c ModelCondition entries, read by a parser of their own whose
/// format is not described here.
///
/// \see ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for ModelConditionAudioLoopClientBehavior: its list of
///        condition and sound entries.
///
/// Built once per module line by
