/// \class ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Client behavior module registered as
///        "ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior": a sound selector
///        keyed by model condition.
///
/// BFME 2 has three sound selector modules: this one,
/// UpgradeSoundSelectorClientBehavior and RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior.
/// Each one's INI entries accept one shared set of voice and sound fields
/// (\c VoiceSelect, \c VoiceMove, \c VoiceAttack and the other \c Voice
/// fields, then \c SoundMoveStart, \c SoundAmbient and the other \c Sound
/// fields), together with fields of their own. Many of the names, such as
/// \c VoiceSelect, \c VoiceMove, \c SoundMoveStart and \c SoundAmbient, are
/// also voice and sound fields of Zero Hour's \c Object blocks. Others, such
/// as \c VoiceSelectBattle, \c VoiceRetreatToCastle, the \c VoiceEnterState
/// fields, \c SoundImpact and \c SoundCrushing, are not in Zero Hour. Their
/// names suggest that each
/// supplies such a set when its condition holds: here, a model condition.
/// How the engine chooses between selectors and the object's own sounds is
/// not described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Field (ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData, from the
/// retail table): \c SoundState entries. Each entry's parser reads the
/// voice and sound field set above; the rest of its format is not
/// described here.
///
/// \see ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior: its
///        sound state entries.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData
/// and shared by every object of the template.

/// \fn Module *ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for
///        "ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior": creates the module
///        for one drawable.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration, and it is
/// the only direct caller of the class's constructor. The group page
/// describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The thing being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's
///                    ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for
///        "ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior": creates the module
///        data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// for each module line naming the module.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Client behavior module registered as
///        "RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior": a sound selector that applies
///        by chance.
///
/// The module keeps a random roll between 0 and 1 and the frame it was
/// made on. RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior::getSelectedValue first calls
/// RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior::reroll, then answers "not selected"
/// when the roll is not below \c Chance; otherwise it hands back the
/// \c VoicePriority value and returns whether \c VoicePriority was given.
/// The reroll draws a new value only when \c RerollOnEveryFrame is set, a
/// game client exists and a counter read from TheGameClient (the
/// reconstruction treats it as the client frame) has changed since the last
/// roll; it uses the client random stream (GameClientRandomValueReal), so
/// it never disturbs the logic random stream that lockstep play depends on
/// (\ref page_core_frameworks_random). Where the first roll is made is not
/// described here.
///
/// RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior::xfer saves the roll and the frame.
/// See ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior for the three sound
/// selectors together.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Fields (RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData, from the retail
/// tables): \c Chance (a percentage, stored as a fraction),
/// \c RerollOnEveryFrame (a boolean), \c UnitSpecificSounds (read by the
/// same parser as the other \c UnitSpecificSounds fields in retail; Zero Hour
/// has a field of that name in \c Object blocks; its format is not described
/// here), \c VoicePriority (an integer,
/// RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::parseVoicePriority), and
/// the whole voice and sound field set described on the
/// ModelConditionSoundSelectorClientBehavior page.
///
/// \see RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior: chance, reroll
///        switch, voice priority and a complete voice and sound set.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and
/// shared by every object of the template. It is by far the largest data
/// class in this group because it embeds the full voice and sound set.

/// \fn Module *RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for
///        "RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior": creates the module for one
///        drawable.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The thing being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's
///                    RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *RandomSoundSelectorClientBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior":
///        creates the module data and parses the module's INI block into
///        it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// for each module line naming the module, and it is the only direct
/// caller of the data class's constructor. The class's
/// \c buildFieldParse adds two tables: its own four fields and the shared
/// voice and sound field set.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see RandomSoundSelectorClientBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance


