/// \class BeaconClientUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Client update module registered as "BeaconClientUpdate": gives a
///        beacon its particle effect and pulses it on the radar.
///
/// BeaconClientUpdate::clientUpdate creates the beacon's particle system
/// the first time it runs. Then, as in Zero Hour, while a drawable
/// visibility test allows it (Zero Hour: the drawable is not effectively
/// hidden), it adds a beacon-pulse radar event at the drawable's position
/// once more than \c RadarPulseFrequency logic frames have passed since the
/// last pulse, lasting \c RadarPulseDuration. Unlike Zero Hour, when that test does not
/// allow a pulse, the BFME 2 body also makes the drawable unselectable,
/// removes it from the in-game UI's selection and lowers it to a height of
/// -100. BeaconClientUpdate::hideBeacon hides the drawable, then calls a
/// further drawable switch with false at the point where Zero Hour turns off
/// shadows (its identity is not established). It also makes the drawable
/// unselectable, deselects it and sets a flag on its particle system,
/// creating that system first if needed. Zero Hour's version hides the
/// drawable, turns off its shadows and stops the particle system; where Zero
/// Hour stops the system, BFME 2 sets that flag instead.
///
/// BeaconClientUpdate::xfer saves the module's state.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Fields (BeaconClientUpdateModuleData, from the retail table):
/// \c RadarPulseFrequency and \c RadarPulseDuration, both durations (see
/// the group page). They are the same two fields Zero Hour has.
///
/// \see BeaconClientUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class BeaconClientUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for BeaconClientUpdate: radar pulse interval and
///        duration.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// BeaconClientUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every
/// object of the template.

/// \fn ModuleData *BeaconClientUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "BeaconClientUpdate": creates the
///        module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// for each module line naming the module. The matching instance factory,
/// BeaconClientUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance, has the shared shape
/// described on the group page.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see BeaconClientUpdate


/// \class RadarMarkerClientUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_create_client_module_factories
/// \brief Client update module registered as "RadarMarkerClientUpdate":
///        keeps a radar marker of a named type at its drawable's position.
///
/// On its client update (the reconstruction names the function
/// RadarMarkerClientUpdate::clientUpdate after Zero Hour's client update
/// slot; the name is inferred), the module needs a drawable. The first time
/// it runs with a radar present, it asks TheRadar for a marker of the type
/// named by \c MarkerType and keeps it; every run then hands the marker the
/// drawable's current position. How the radar draws the marker is not
/// described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Field (RadarMarkerClientUpdateModuleData, from the retail table):
/// \c MarkerType, a name stored as text and passed to the radar when the
/// marker is first made.
///
